determinant(MultidimensionalMatrix) -- hyperdeterminant of a multidimensional matrix
************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note determinant: (Macaulay2Doc)determinant,
  * Usage: 
        det M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note multidimensional matrix: MultidimensionalMatrix,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Strategy: (Macaulay2Doc)determinant_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_
        pd_pd_rp, => ..., default value null,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the hyperdeterminant
        of $M$

Description
===========

This is calculated using Schlafli's method where it is known to work. Use an
optional input as Strategy=>"forceSchlafliMethod" to try to force this approach
(but without ensuring the correctness of the calculation). For matrices of
boundary shape, the calculation passes through *note
sylvesterMatrix(MultidimensionalMatrix):
sylvesterMatrix_lpMultidimensionalMatrix_rp,. For details, see the Chapter 14
in the book Discriminants, Resultants, and Multidimensional Determinants (see
http://link.springer.com/book/10.1007%2F978-0-8176-4771-1 ).

