exponentsMatrix -- exponents in one or more polynomials
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        exponentsMatrix(f_0,f_1,...)
  * Inputs:
      * (f_0,f_1,...) one or more Laurent polynomials in the same ring.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Unmixed => ..., default value null
  * Outputs:
      * (A_0,A_1,...) a sequence of matrices such that the columns of A_i are
        the *note exponents: (Macaulay2Doc)exponents, of f_i. If either the
        option Unmixed is set to true or all the matrices A_i are equal, then
        just one matrix is returned whose columns are all the exponents
        occurring in at least one of the polynomials.

Description
===========

+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : QQ[x,y,z];                                             |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = (x^2 - 7 + x*y*z^11 + y, -3*y^7*z + x^3*y + 5*x^2);|
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : exponentsMatrix(f_0)                                   |
|                                                            |
|o3 = | 0 0 1  2 |                                           |
|     | 0 1 1  0 |                                           |
|     | 0 0 11 0 |                                           |
|                                                            |
|              3       4                                     |
|o3 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                      |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : exponentsMatrix(f_0,f_1)                               |
|                                                            |
|o4 = (| 0 0 1  2 |, | 0 2 3 |)                              |
|      | 0 1 1  0 |  | 7 0 1 |                               |
|      | 0 0 11 0 |  | 1 0 0 |                               |
|                                                            |
|o4 : Sequence                                               |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : exponentsMatrix(f_0,f_1,Unmixed=>true)                 |
|                                                            |
|o5 = | 0 0 0 1  2 3 |                                       |
|     | 0 1 7 1  0 1 |                                       |
|     | 0 0 1 11 0 0 |                                       |
|                                                            |
|              3       6                                     |
|o5 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                      |
+------------------------------------------------------------+

