genericLaurentPolynomials -- generic (Laurent) polynomials
**********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        genericLaurentPolynomials A
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, or a *note list:
        (Macaulay2Doc)List, of $n+1$ matrices $A_0,\ldots,A_n$ over
        $\mathbb{Z}$ and with $n$ rows to represent the exponent vectors of
        (Laurent) polynomials $f_0,\ldots,f_n$ in $n$ variables. For the dense
        case, one can pass just the sequence of degrees of $f_0,\ldots,f_n$.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * CoefficientRing => ..., default value ZZ
  * Outputs:
      * the generic (Laurent) polynomials $f_0,\ldots,f_n$ in the ring
        $\mathbb{Z}[a_0,a_1,\ldots,b_0,b_1,\ldots][x_1,\ldots,x_n]$, involving
        only the monomials from $A$. (Note that, if all the exponents are
        nonnegative, then the ambient polynomial ring is taken without inverses
        of variables, so that $f_0,\ldots,f_n$ are ordinary polynomials.)

Description
===========

This method helps to construct special types of sparse resultants, see for
instance *note denseResultant: denseResultant,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = (matrix{{2,3,4,5},{0,2,1,0}},matrix{{1,-1,0,2,3},{-2,0,-7,-1,0}},   |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = (| 2 3 4 5 |, | 1  -1 0  2  3 |, | -1 0 6 |)                            |
|      | 0 2 1 0 |  | -2 0  -7 -1 0 |  | -2 1 3 |                             |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : Sequence                                                                |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|matrix{{-1,0,6},{-2,1,3}})                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : genericLaurentPolynomials M                                             |
|                                                                             |
|         5      4        3 2      2     3      2 -1        -2      -7        |
|o2 = (a x  + a x x  + a x x  + a x , b x  + b x x   + b x x   + b x   +      |
|       3 1    2 1 2    1 1 2    0 1   4 1    3 1 2     2 1 2     1 2         |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|        -1     6 3             -1 -2                                         |
|     b x  , c x x  + c x  + c x  x  )                                        |
|      0 1    2 1 2    1 2    0 1  2                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Sequence                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : genericLaurentPolynomials (2,3,1)                                       |
|                                                                             |
|         2               2                        3      2          2      3 |
|o3 = (a x  + a x x  + a x  + a x  + a x  + a , b x  + b x x  + b x x  + b x  |
|       5 1    4 1 2    2 2    3 1    1 2    0   9 1    8 1 2    6 1 2    3 2 |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|          2               2                                                  |
|     + b x  + b x x  + b x  + b x  + b x  + b , c x  + c x  + c )            |
|        7 1    5 1 2    2 2    4 1    1 2    0   2 1    1 2    0             |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Sequence                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

