permute -- permute the dimensions of a multidimensional matrix
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        permute(M,s)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note multidimensional matrix: MultidimensionalMatrix,, an
        $n$-dimensional matrix.
      * s, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a permutation of the set
        $\{0,1,\ldots,n-1\}$.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note multidimensional matrix: MultidimensionalMatrix,, with the same
        entries as the input, but with the dimensions re-ordered according to
        the specified permutation.

Description
===========

According to the definition given on page 449 of the book Discriminants,
Resultants, and Multidimensional Determinants (see
http://link.springer.com/book/10.1007%2F978-0-8176-4771-1 ), the output of this
method is $s'(M)$, where $s'$ is the inverse permutation of $s$.

