rank(MultidimensionalMatrix) -- about the border rank of a multidimensional matrix
**********************************************************************************

  * Function: *note rank: (Macaulay2Doc)rank,
  * Usage: 
        rank M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note multidimensional matrix: MultidimensionalMatrix,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a lower bound for the (border)
        rank of M, which is calculated as the maximum rank of all the *note
        flattenings: flattening, of M

Description
===========

In some cases, we know that the returned integer r = rank M is exactly the
border rank of M. For instance, this is the case if r<3 by a result of C. Raicu
(see https://arxiv.org/abs/1011.5867v2 ). In general, however, we obtain only a
lower bound and it is not known how to calculate this rank exactly without
resorting to elimination.

