sparseDiscriminant -- sparse discriminant (A-discriminant)
**********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        sparseDiscriminant A
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a matrix over $\mathbb{Z}$
        with $n$ rows to represent the exponent vectors of a Laurent polynomial
        $f$ in $n$ variables, $f = \sum_{\omega\in A} a_{\omega} x^{\omega}$.
        If one wants to perform computations only in characteristic $p>0$, then
        it is recommended to use the option CoefficientRing=>ZZ/p.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * CoefficientRing => ..., default value ZZ
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note SparseDiscriminant: SparseDiscriminant,,
        the universal sparse discriminant associated to $A$, that is, a
        function that to a Laurent polynomial $f$ in $n$ variables over a
        coefficient ring $K$, involving only monomials from $A$, associates the
        sparse discriminant of $f$, which is an element of $K$.

Description
===========

Alternatively, one can apply the method directly to the Laurent polynomial $f$.
In this case, the matrix $A$ is automatically determined by *note
exponentsMatrix: exponentsMatrix,.

As an example, we now calculate the sparse discriminant of a generic trilinear
form on $\mathbb{P}^1\times\mathbb{P}^2\times \mathbb{P}^1$, that is, the
hyperdeterminant of a generic three-dimensional matrix of shape $2\times
3\times 2$.

