SparseResultant -- the class of all sparse resultants
*****************************************************

Description
===========

An object of this class is created by the method *note sparseResultant:
sparseResultant,, when the input is given by $n+1$ integral matrices
$A_0,\ldots,A_n$ with $n$ rows. Such an object behaves like a function that to
$n+1$ Laurent polynomials $f_0,\ldots,f_n$ in $n$ variables
$x=(x_1,\ldots,x_n)$, with $f_i = \sum_{\omega\in \{columns\ of\ A_i\}}
a_{i,\omega} x^{\omega}$, associates their sparse resultant
$Res_{A_0,\ldots,A_n}(f_0,\ldots,f_n)$, which is a polynomial in the
coefficients $a_{i,\omega}$. An error is thrown if the polynomials $f_i$ do not
have the correct form.

Functions and methods returning an object of class SparseResultant:
===================================================================

  * *note sparseResultant: sparseResultant, -- sparse resultant (A-resultant)

Methods that use an object of class SparseResultant:
====================================================

  * *note char(SparseResultant): char_lpSparseResultant_rp, -- get the
    characteristic
  * *note exponents(SparseResultant): exponents_lpSparseResultant_rp, -- get
    the matrices of exponents
  * *note SparseResultant Thing: SparseResultant Thing, -- evaluate a sparse
    resultant

For the programmer
==================

The object *note SparseResultant: SparseResultant, is a *note type:
(Macaulay2Doc)Type,, with ancestor classes *note HashTable:
(Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, < *note Thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,.

